# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exit survey submission — OPTIONAL, and off by default.
#
# Leave both of these unset and the course makes no network requests at all:
# every student's progress, answers and licence stay on their own device, which
# is how the pilot runs unless a teacher decides otherwise.
#
# Set VITE_SURVEY_ENDPOINT and only the exit survey is posted, once, when a
# student presses Finish. Nothing else is ever sent — not module answers, not
# question-by-question history, not names, emails, student ids or device
# details. See README, "Collecting exit-survey results", for the full field
# list and for what each hosting option means for privacy.
#
# These are build-time values baked into the JavaScript bundle, so treat the
# endpoint URL as public. Never put an API key, token or password in a VITE_
# variable: anyone who opens the site can read it. Use a service that accepts
# unauthenticated posts to a URL that is unguessable, and set it in the Vercel
# dashboard rather than committing it here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Must be https (http is only accepted for localhost while testing).
# VITE_SURVEY_ENDPOINT=https://example.com/your-unguessable-collection-url

# Optional label so a teacher can tell classes apart. Never a student identifier.
# VITE_SURVEY_CLASS_ID=period-3
